            <div xml:id="d348">

                <pb facs="0479" n="394" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg394"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00/2102: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul in Charge of the Legation in Honduras</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Lawton</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-10-30T20:00:00-05:48"><hi rendition="#italic">October 30,
                                1919, 8 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received
                            November 1, 10.30 p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>General Gutierrez elected President 76,000 votes to 18,000 votes for Membreño. No
                    serious difficulties occurred during the election. Conditions are quiet.
                    Membreño arrived at Amapala today. I have given my opinion to President Bogran
                    that Membreno cannot now demand the Presidency as Vice President and that Bogran
                    must remain in the chair until formally delivered to President elect. I would
                    like instructions on this subject.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lawton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
